#, fuzzy
msgid "Your deployment target expects a single file (for example, a legacy application server, a simple deployment script, or a `java -jar` invocation with no additional classpath setup)."
msgstr "您的部署目标要求仅提供一个文件（例如，传统应用服务器、简单的部署脚本，或者无需额外配置类路径的 ` `java -jar` ` 调用）。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "You want to copy a single artifact to a remote server without worrying about directory structure."
msgstr "您希望将单个工件复制到远程服务器，且无需考虑目录结构。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "The trade-offs compared to the fast JAR are:"
msgstr "与快速 JAR 相比，其权衡之处在于："

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flat structure. The uber-JAR merges all dependencies into a single archive, losing the original JAR boundaries. This can cause issues with resources that have the same path across multiple dependencies. JAR signatures from signed dependencies are also lost in the process."
msgstr "扁平化结构。uber-JAR 将所有依赖项合并到一个归档文件中，从而消除了原始 JAR 的边界。这可能会导致在多个依赖项中路径相同的资源出现问题。在此过程中，已签名的依赖项的 JAR 签名也会丢失。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "No container image layering. With the fast JAR, container image builders like Jib can cache dependency JARs in a separate layer so that only the thin application layer changes on rebuild. An uber-JAR is a single file, so the entire image layer must be rebuilt and pushed on every change."
msgstr "不采用容器镜像分层机制。使用快速 JAR 时，Jib 等容器镜像构建工具可以将依赖项 JAR 缓存到单独的层中，这样在重新构建时，只有轻量级的应用程序层会发生变化。而 uber-JAR 是一个单一文件，因此每次发生变化时，都必须重新构建并推送整个镜像层。"

